# OS command injection: a shell/exec sink called with a NON-literal argument.
# Promoted from the learn loop (LEARNED-1789846034-7): matches the dangerous
# sinks but uses `exclude` (pattern-not) to suppress the safe case where the
# argument is a bare string literal — match broad, subtract the safe case.
# Target narrowed to code extensions on promotion.
id: KEUR-CMDI-001
title: OS command injection — shell sink with a non-literal argument
category: cmdi
severity: critical
engine: pattern
action: block
target:
  extensions: .js .php .rb .py .ts .go .java
patterns:
  - regex: (?i)\b(?:subprocess\.run|os\.system|exec\.[^ ]+|`[^`]*`)\s*\([^)]*[^"'\s]\S*[^"'\s][^)]*\)
    exclude: \b(?:subprocess\.run|os\.system|exec\.[^ ]+|`[^`]*`)\s*\([^)]*["'][^"']+["'][^)]*\)
    message: A shell/exec sink is called with a non-literal (variable) argument — potential OS command injection (CWE-78). Pass a fixed argument vector or validate/escape the input.
confidence: 0.9
fix: Use a parameterised argument vector (no shell string interpolation), or strictly validate/escape the input before it reaches the sink.
